{
  "schema": "semio.quiz.crowd-client/v1",
  "description": "What the others think, as the web client shows it (design §17). A crowd is live while anyone else thinks along in the quiz (one learner per tag, counted by distinct tags), else the submitted runs once there is one, else none. Live item crowds come from the others' drafts aggregated for the viewer's sheet task, submitted ones from the crowd view; both are keyed by item id in the viewer's sheet order (the submitted view's order for submitted crowds). Choices by category or value are ordered by count descending, then by value numerically when both keys are numbers, else by code point — a crowd view's keys arrive in code point order (`120` before `8`) and are re-sorted for display. Positions of a sorting are normalized (0 smallest … 1 largest), live one per learner by tag, submitted their mean; the place shown is `1 + position × (total − 1)` to one decimal. A draft is the learner's own answer in the form peers read: classification and sorting unchanged, matching card indices replaced by the card values; an answer that does not fit its sheet task is no draft.",
